[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4891302720","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120985#issuecomment-4891302720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120985","id":4891302720,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4tbQA","user":{"login":"Bromeon","id":708488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwODQ4OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/708488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Bromeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bromeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T09:39:27Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T09:39:27Z","body":"> where the parent classes aren't auto-exposed by an exposed child class being registered.\r\n\r\nI'm missing a bit of context here, but are we sure that auto-exposing is a good practice?\r\n\r\nIf I register a hidden (internal) class, I don't want it to become visible because someone else inherits it.\r\nThis violates my original intent. It would be more intuitive if inheriting is only allowed if that class is _also_ hidden.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4891302720/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4891362083","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120985#issuecomment-4891362083","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120985","id":4891362083,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4xDIw","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T09:45:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T09:45:49Z","body":"> If I register a hidden (internal) class, I don't want it to become visible because someone else inherits it. This violates my original intent. It would be more intuitive if inheriting is only allowed if that class is _also_ hidden.\r\n\r\n\"exposed\" in this case means \"documented and visible\". If we would not force `exposed = true` on the parent when a child registers, it could create a situation where a child has methods (from its parent) that are not documented but still bound and accessible.\r\n\r\nIf you want the parent to be restricted, you can either make it a [`GDSOFTCLASS`](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/engine_details/architecture/object_class.html#registering-object-classes) (which will not expose it at all and strips the ability to register custom methods on it), or make it `virtual` or `abstract`.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4891362083/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4891371325","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120985#issuecomment-4891371325","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120985","id":4891371325,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4xnPQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-06T09:46:50Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T09:46:50Z","body":"If we wanted to honor the parent instead of forcing it to be exposed, we could also reject subclassing (with an exposed class) if the superclass is not exposed. However, that's a different discussion